# ★★★ DURABLE DEPLOYMENT DEFAULT FOR THE WEEKLY TRUST BATCH (2026-08-14).
#
# `trust-cron-host.sh` reads this file automatically as a FALLBACK — ONLY
# when `RECSYS_TRUST_SINCE_DAYS` is not already set in the shell that runs
# it. A value exported in the operator's own shell always wins over anything
# here; this file exists purely to stop the value being lost when nobody's
# shell has it, which is exactly what happened before this file existed: the
# window lived only in whichever operator's memory/history last set it.
#
# Unlike `.env.local` (this repo's real secrets file, excluded by
# `.gitignore`'s `.env.*` rule), this file is a plain committed config file —
# deliberately NOT named `.env.*` so it ships with every checkout instead of
# being ignored. Copy nothing: `trust-cron-host.sh` reads it directly from
# `deploy/` next to itself.
#
# ★★★ WHY 90, NOT THE 365-DAY DEFAULT (`settings.history.trust_days`).
# Measured 2026-08-14 against the public HAFSQL mirror (see
# `trust-cron-host.sh`'s own header for the full timing table): the 365-day
# window cannot complete at all (cancelled at 900s, and again at 3600s) — the
# planner flips from a per-block Nested Loop to a Merge Join that index-scans
# every comment operation ever made. 90 days completed in 29.7s in the same
# measurement. Re-measure before raising this on a fresh mirror or replica;
# do not assume the number travels with the deployment unchanged.
RECSYS_TRUST_SINCE_DAYS=90
